      "topic": "Area between curves",
      "type": "long",
      "marks": 5,
      "q": "Find the area of the region bounded by the parabola $y^2=4x$ and the line $y=2x-4$.",
      "solution": "Write both as $x$ in terms of $y$: $x=\\dfrac{y^2}{4}$ and $x=\\dfrac{y+4}{2}$.\n\nThey meet where $\\dfrac{y^2}{4}=\\dfrac{y+4}{2}$, i.e. $y^2-2y-8=0$, so $y=-2$ and $y=4$.\n\nBetween them the line lies to the right of the parabola, so\n\nArea $=\\displaystyle\\int_{-2}^{4}\\left(\\frac{y+4}{2}-\\frac{y^2}{4}\\right)dy=\\left[\\frac{y^2}{4}+2y-\\frac{y^3}{12}\\right]_{-2}^{4}$\n\n$=\\left(4+8-\\dfrac{16}{3}\\right)-\\left(1-4+\\dfrac23\\right)=\\dfrac{20}{3}+\\dfrac73=9$ square units."
